TITLE:: RAOutputChain
summary:: An ambisonic output chain: signal → transformer → inserted stages → decoder, each a NodeProxy in its own Group
categories:: Libraries>reAmbi
related:: Guides/reAmbi, Classes/RAStereoMonitor, Classes/RCSong

DESCRIPTION::
The monitoring chain of a piece as an object: a strong::signal:: proxy the instruments write to, an optional identity strong::transformer::, any number of inserted stages (reverbs, all-pass, dry-outs) and a strong::decoder:: (AmbiX matrix, binaural HRTF convolution, or raw) played on an output bus. Registered on a song with link::Classes/RCSong#-addOutput:: and built by link::Classes/RCSong#-buildOutputs:: after the node tree exists.

The constructor allocates nothing: the server resets its allocators at every boot, so buses and proxies are made in code::build::. Until then the configuration (code::numChannels::, code::order::, code::outBus::, code::decode::) is already valid for the instrument files.

code::build:: is synchronous and race-free: one Group per stage created in order (message order is node order: no moves, no waits), each proxy placed in its group with code::group_::, the stages linked (nodeMaps only, before any synth exists), then the sources and the decoder's monitor into a play group after the stages. With the server stopped it builds client-side and sends nothing (tests, NRT). code::insert::, code::remove:: and code::move:: re-map only the links they touch, so the other stages keep playing (a full rewire would cut reverb tails). code::clear:: frees the groups first (immediate code::/n_free::) and then the proxies, so nothing delayed reaches a dead node: link::Classes/RCSong#-clearAll:: can free the parent group right after.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: server
argument:: order
Ambisonic order (3 → 16 channels).
argument:: name
argument:: decode
code::\ambix:: (link::Classes/HoaMatrixDecoder::), code::\binaural:: (link::Classes/HOABinaural::, IRs loaded per order with a completion callback) or code::\raw:: (identity, for conversion rigs).
argument:: outBus
argument:: play
Whether the decoder is played on outBus.
argument:: useTransformer
An identity transformer stage after the signal (the pieces set its source to a filter live).
argument:: headphoneModel
link::Classes/HOABinaural:: headphone correction index, or nil.
argument:: refRadius
AmbiX near-field decoding radius.
argument:: binauralRadius
Binaural near-field decoding radius.
argument:: foaRefRadius
Kept for the pieces' FOA effects.
argument:: fadeTime
Proxy fade time.
argument:: placeholder
A faint circling pink noise as the signal's initial source.

METHOD:: loadBinauralIRs
argument:: server
argument:: order
argument:: action
Loads the IRs of one order (the quark loads all seven with no callback); action runs once the last buffer is in. A server reboot forgets the cache.
METHOD:: binauralReady
argument:: server
argument:: order

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: build
argument:: parentGroup
The group the stage groups are created in (the song's code::\outputDecode:: group). Returns this.
METHOD:: clear
Back to the unbuilt configuration; inserted stages and taps are dropped, the monitor stays registered.
METHOD:: isBuilt
METHOD:: isOffline
True when the last build happened with the server stopped.

METHOD:: numChannels
code::(order + 1).squared::, valid before build.
METHOD:: playChannels
2 for binaural, code::numChannels:: otherwise (the scope lines).

METHOD:: signal
METHOD:: transformer
METHOD:: decoder
The stage NodeProxies (nil before build; transformer nil when unused).
METHOD:: stages
Ordered Array of code::[name, proxy]::.
METHOD:: stageNames
METHOD:: stage
argument:: stageName
METHOD:: lastStage
The stage feeding the decoder.
METHOD:: bus
argument:: stageName
The proxy bus of a stage (code::\monitor:: for the stereo monitor's), for recorders.

METHOD:: insert
argument:: stageName
argument:: source
A Function (or any proxy source: the chain makes and owns the proxy) or an existing NodeProxy (adopted).
argument:: after
argument:: before
Stage names; default right before the decoder. Returns the stage proxy. Before build the stage is recorded and realized by build.
METHOD:: remove
argument:: stageName
argument:: fadeTime
METHOD:: move
argument:: stageName
argument:: after
argument:: before

METHOD:: tap
argument:: tapName
argument:: proxy
argument:: from
A stage name, or code::\last::: the stage feeding the decoder, followed across inserts, removes and moves. Maps the proxy's code::\in::.
METHOD:: untap
argument:: tapName
METHOD:: addMonitor
argument:: monitor
An link::Classes/RAStereoMonitor::, built now if the chain is, rebuilt with every build.
METHOD:: monitor
METHOD:: removeMonitor

METHOD:: decode
METHOD:: outBus
METHOD:: play
METHOD:: useTransformer
METHOD:: headphoneModel
METHOD:: refRadius
METHOD:: binauralRadius
METHOD:: foaRefRadius
METHOD:: fadeTime
METHOD:: placeholder
Configuration; the setters take effect at the next build (code::useTransformer_:: needs an unbuilt chain).

EXAMPLES::

code::
(
~song.addOutput(\main, RAOutputChain(s, 3, \main, decode: \ambix, outBus: 0));
~song.makeGroups;
~song.buildOutputs;     // synchronous
)
~song.ambi.signal.source = { HOAEncoder.ar(3, PinkNoise.ar(0.1), 0, 0) };
~reverb = ~song.ambi.insert(\reverb, { var in = \in.ar(0 ! 16); in + FreeVerb.ar(in, 0.3) });
~song.ambi.addMonitor(RAStereoMonitor(16, 18));
~song.ambi.remove(\reverb);
~song.clearAll;
::
